  "summary": "Phase 5 implements the exact version-2 no-wait rule-acceptance profile, phase-bound upstream authority, durable settlement baselines, autonomous commit proof, and bounded baseline refresh. The accepted review defect was fixed: refresh eligibility now compares the settlement-time configuration digest with one freshly materialized live configuration snapshot, and exact retained document bytes and Git mode are rechecked before refresh. Focused authority and semantic suites, typechecking, schema checks, unit, contract, integration, crash, release reproducibility, and diff checks passed; the fresh independent counter-review reported no material findings. One evidence limitation remains explicit by user direction: the authenticated real-host selection check was not rerun because it would invoke external Claude/Codex hosts, so that evidence is omitted rather than represented as passing.",
